  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_af5a62adb0954433918f6521d9725610",
      "statement": "frontend/mcm-app/server.js is the BFF's production entrypoint: a CommonJS Express adapter that requires @expo/server/adapter/express, hands the exported dist/server bundle to createRequestHandler, and serves dist/client as static assets; because it runs outside the Metro bundle it cannot require anything from src/, which is why scheduled work reaches the bundle through a loopback HTTP call instead of a function call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/README.md#L156-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6070338f8608d8e3f8ae3f38710b92e9457de4393f9202dc0cda92662bec848:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L1-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ca21bf6a540fabc4e00c97644a8d4f5cbf1b91cb92e4eea586e8995a1757501:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f81c986389f04043986929e9c049874d",
      "statement": "server.js pre-seeds `globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry = { url: pathToFileURL(__filename).href }` before createRequestHandler loads the bundle, because Metro rewrites `import.meta.url` in bundled dependencies to `globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry.url` and the exported @expo/server runtime — unlike the Metro dev server — never populates that registry; the `if (!globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry)` guard is intentional so a future @expo/server version that populates it makes the line a no-op rather than being clobbered.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L13-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cab8e34974fbd978268f9362c58b40fe704fee3d1fd4c0c962d8e0d8943409c0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_994404f4df094fb5b79cd494685770eb",
      "statement": "Without the registry seeding, any bundled dependency calling `createRequire(import.meta.url)` — @copilotkit/runtime's lazily-required adapter on the /bff-api/agent/run path — throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'url')` asynchronously inside the streaming respond pipeline, so the route's own try/catch never sees it: the client hangs with no 500 and no log line, in the container only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L13-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cab8e34974fbd978268f9362c58b40fe704fee3d1fd4c0c962d8e0d8943409c0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/agent/run%2Bapi.ts#L255-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfeaba2376c740975ebe821eeb8a1aefcd8e9dec5da2031be7f0baac9c7504c5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e30fceff011f438eab2f6a8dd478a5e6",
      "statement": "The same lazy require is a build-time consequence: because the specifier is a bare string passed to createRequire(globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry.url), a static closure walk cannot see it, so the BFF image build re-derives the dynamic specifiers from the freshly exported dist/server and fails when one is not accounted for in the prune script's known-specifier map.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/Dockerfile#L54-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4da8067df0735ad06d4d7f926c0d7b401bd5731e100f03499eab5e5a1bb0e5d3:"
        },
