          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:067902bbf43714c178be4b3edfd362f620d9db07030d83a10e14827dcbb277e8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/prune-bff-runtime-modules.mjs#L52-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69767b6904f019c07f0e301ba63696c3250257844428433f24f7bf80aa9727f6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0439f85385e34bbc8df8db6ab4f935b6",
      "statement": "Under express 5 (path-to-regexp v8) the Expo catch-all must be the named, braced route `'/{*splat}'`: a bare `'*'` is rejected at BOOT with `Missing parameter name at index 1: *` while routes are being registered, so the process never reaches app.listen, and the braces make the wildcard optional so `/` itself still matches.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L105-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9876bc4c4bb70d15efe1f7e7c7e6a86737e00292422c2a74d167ef63b8d908c4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dbd34362dee74a0981616071755ff549",
      "statement": "The catch-all uses `app.all` rather than `app.use` deliberately: a route decodes its params, so a malformed percent-encoded path such as `/bff-api/%E0%A4%A` is answered 400 by express before the Expo handler sees it, and the single registration forwards every method and the raw query string (bracket syntax included) for both the /bff-api API surface and the SSR pages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L105-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9876bc4c4bb70d15efe1f7e7c7e6a86737e00292422c2a74d167ef63b8d908c4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/unit/bff-server-adapter.test.ts#L108-L134",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e967760c69542866452a9021d9ca30b2e369da33bef41198b8a13e9c455af6e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c2ca321b421451b81e340b2aa456c26",
      "statement": "Static serving selects between two express.static instances on the last DECODED segment of the request path (a dotfile-last path goes to the default `ignore` instance, everything else to a `dotfiles: 'allow'` one), and an undecodable path falls to the strict instance — so a dotfile inside a dot-directory is not served, `/%2Eenv` counts as a dotfile because send decodes before it checks, and files inside dot-directories are served.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L73-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10ff292d7b43c17ad16c63a7ac28881f393c11853c03ed782271f833ab12f175:"
        },
        {
