    {
      "id": "claim_e872d3ca747f4a23959b4de1df13a95d",
      "statement": "tests/unit/bff-server-adapter.test.ts is the pin for the express layer: it copies the real server.js and web-security-headers.js into a temp directory beside a fixture dist/client and boots it in a child process with only @expo/server/adapter/express replaced by a `node -r` preload that echoes what express delivered, with express resolved from the package's own node_modules via NODE_PATH — the only test that exercises server.js, since the unit tier imports TS modules and the integration tier calls route handlers directly.",
