          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2a4396bc75a9839223407818e71389a442fb0d55ba69e234bd3f08081594c0c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L90-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b60c758451c7a0749ec01afd48408cbf666b396013d195ce0e18bc8c3a5c47c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_00cd02e0628e4a34ac75a7fe99bc2bd8",
      "statement": "A second, distinct recovery in the same wrapper handles a THROWN transport error on the agent route only: it waits RUN_RETRY_DELAY_MS (250 ms) for a reset tunnel to re-establish and retries exactly once, which is safe because a dropped connection aborts the upstream gateway turn via @expo/server's AbortController, making the cut turn idempotent-on-failure; non-agent throws propagate unchanged and a genuine 4xx returns a Response so it is never retried.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L38-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b45e0d873fad5ba64a377c51eff88bc94ab64098f3715357b681e94b1de1d232:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/unit-tests/agent-fetch-refresh.test.ts#L83-L138",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d8bd222177561c249ab258df5e24c2633d6562f655999ef8ae2cf0ea08c79bb2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b1bbbcd0202044baaf2881096d81c857",
      "statement": "Neither recovery loops: a still-401 response after a successful refresh is returned as-is, a failed refresh returns the original 401 with no retry, and a second consecutive throw is propagated — so the 401 path and the transport-drop path are each capped at one retry, and createRefreshingFetch is a pure factory taking an injected baseFetch + refresh so both paths are unit-tested without any global.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L51-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d3e662a3f57dfcadc9a25f88cf95f6d164482af3664ca2e146a0b0b4f84b816:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/unit-tests/agent-fetch-refresh.test.ts#L16-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24356cd9c8b3b6bb608a02c4919ca9cb3095eb53e1399f19da35751850b40448:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2f80c85bc54947e884df44caf53e4018",
      "statement": "assistant-polyfills.native.ts is ordered so the refresh wrapper is installed after the CopilotKit crypto and streaming polyfills and before any CopilotKit run — the crypto polyfill, then @copilotkit/react-native/polyfills, then installAgentFetchRefresh() — and its `require` calls are deliberately inline rather than hoisted imports so the LogBox ignore for the crypto polyfill's import-time warning is registered first; the order must not be changed.",
